# S12-T04: Ephemeral Tab Identity (pre-auth)

## App-agent preflight

- [ ] `explain("work-control")` — auth note (S15 = real identity)
- [ ] Read `S12-INVARIANTS.md` §4 — ephemeral ID spec

## Implementation

Create `apps/work-control/app/composables/usePresenceId.ts`:

```ts
// Generates a stable per-tab random ID (UUID v4, stored in sessionStorage).
// After S15 auth, this is replaced by the real user session ID.
// The label is "User " + last 4 chars of the id for anonymous display.

export function usePresenceId() {
  const KEY = 'wc-presence-id'

  const id = (() => {
    if (import.meta.server) return ''
    let stored = sessionStorage.getItem(KEY)
    if (!stored) {
      stored = crypto.randomUUID()
      sessionStorage.setItem(KEY, stored)
    }
    return stored
  })()

  const label = `User ${id.slice(-4).toUpperCase()}`

  return { id, label }
}
```

Extend `useRealtime.ts`:
- Accept optional `member?: PresenceMember` param
- Include `member` in the `subscribe` message sent to server
- Expose `members: Ref<PresenceMember[]>` that updates on `presence.sync` events

```ts
// In useRealtime:
export function useRealtime(room: MaybeRefOrGetter<string | string[]>, member?: PresenceMember) {
  const members = ref<PresenceMember[]>([])
  // ...in message handler:
  if (data.type === 'presence.sync') {
    members.value = data.members
  }
  // ...in subscribe():
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'subscribe', rooms: roomList(), member }))
  return { connected, on, members }
}
```

## Done when

- [ ] `usePresenceId()` returns stable UUID across reactive renders (not new ID on re-render)
- [ ] Two tabs generate different IDs (sessionStorage isolation)
- [ ] `useRealtime` `members` ref updates when `presence.sync` received
- [ ] `bun run test` — composable unit tests
